prompt:
Implement the linker's archive scan as a function:

```c
typedef struct { int defines[8]; size_t ndefs; } member_t;
int member_pulls(const member_t *m, const int *pending, size_t npending);
```

Return 1 iff any of the member's defined symbols appears in the pending list — the pull-in rule from module 10, now executable against arbitrary tables.

tests.code:
member_t m = {{0}};
int d[2] = {30, 31};
m.ndefs = 2;
m.defines[0] = 30;
m.defines[1] = 31;
int pend[2] = {31, 44};
CHECK_EQ(member_pulls(&m, pend, 2), 1);

member_t m2 = {{0}};
int d2[1] = {90};
m2.ndefs = 1;
m2.defines[0] = 90;
int pend2[1] = {31};
CHECK_EQ(member_pulls(&m2, pend2, 1), 0);
